<!-- shortcodes -->
<div class="typrography">
    <div class="container">
        <h3 class="tittle">सभा का सविधान</h3>
        <div class="grid_3 grid_4 wow fadeInLeft animated" data-wow-delay=".5s">
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center; padding-top:30px">
                THE RULES OF THE GARHWAL HITESHINI SABHA
            </h3>
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center">
                (Established 1923)
            </h3>
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center">
                (Corrected upto 10th August, 1941)
            </h3>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><h2 id="h2.-bootstrap-heading" class="bars">Name <a class="anchorjs-link" href="#h1.-bootstrap-heading"><span class="anchorjs-icon"></span></a></h2></td>
                            <td class="type-info"><p style="color:black; font-size:20px">The Sabha (heretofore known as the “Garhwal Sabha Hiteshini Sabha, Shimla, Established 1923”) shall be called “The Garhwal Hiteshini Sabha (Established 1923)”.</p></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><h3 id="h2.-bootstrap-heading" class="bars"> Location</h3></td>
                            <td class="type-info"><p style="color:black; font-size:20px">The registered office of the Sabha shall be in New Delhi but for the convenience of the members of the Sabha moving to Shimla for summer with the Headquarters of the Government of India and those residing permanently at Shimla, a Branch of the Sabha shall function at Shimla throughout the year. </p></td>
                        </tr>
                      
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInRight animated" data-wow-delay=".5s">
            <h2 style="text-align:center">OBJECTS</h2>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info"><p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
    The objects of the Sabha shall be:-

    <br /><br />

    i)                    To promote goodwill and unity amongst Garhwalis,
    <br />
    ii)                  To promote the social and cultural interests of the Garhwalis,
    <br />
    iii)                To open free night schools for the poor and illiterate Garhwalis and to establish regular primary schools so as to impart education to the Garhwali children through the medium of Garhwali vernacular,
    <br />
    iv)                To open free libraries and free dispensaries for the Garhwalis,
    <br />
    v)                  To perpetuate the traditional loyalty of the Garhwalis to the British Government,
    <br />
    vi)                To render financial and other suitable help to Garhwalis in distress in general and Garhwali orphan in particular,
    <br />
    vii)              To subscribe and to contribute from time to time to any charitable benevolent or religious object of a public nature,
    <br />
    viii)            To award scholarships to deserving Garhwali students in various institutions,
    <br />
    ix)                To create a club building in New Delhi to provide recreation and social amenities for Garhwalis and for religious or social lectures and gatherings,
    <br />
    x)                  To maintain a sort of museum containing photos and portraits etc. of the Garhwali soldiers of distinction,
    <br />
    xi)                To do all such other things as are incidental and conducive to the attainment of the above objects or any of them.
</p></td>
                        </tr>
                       
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <div class="clearfix"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInLeft animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h2 class="bars" style="text-align:center">MEMBERSHIP</h2>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    (a)   The membership of the Sabha shall be open to Garhwalis. The Managing Committee may however admit any other person or persons for special reasons.
                                    <br />
                                    (b)   Applications for membership on the Sabha’s prescribed form together with the entrance fee and monthly subscription as laid down in the rule 4 below shall be sent to the General Secretary. The Managing Committee may reject any application for membership, provided it is in the interest of the Sabha to do so without assigning any reason.
                                    <br />
                                    (c)    Members wishing to resign his membership shall notify his intention in writing to the General Secretary. Such registration shall take effect from 1st day of the month following that in which the notification is received.
                                    <br />
                                    (d)   A members seeking readmission shall be required to pay in full his previous dues if any to the Sabha.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInRight animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h2 class="bars" style="text-align:center">ENTRANCE FEE AND SUBSCRIPTION</h2>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    (a)   An entrance fee of annas four shall be payable by all members on admission or re-admission.
                                    <br />
                                    (b)   The minimum monthly subscription shall be anna one.
                                    <br />
                                    (c)    Subscription shall be paid monthly. Any member who is in arrears for six months shall be liable to forfeit membership. The Managing Committee shall have power to waive recovery of subscription from any member or members for special reason upto a period of one year. Recovery of subscription for period beyond one year shall be waived only with the sanction of the General Body.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <p>
                    <b>
                        NOTE:-   Subscriptions may be paid in advance in lump sum at any time for periods of 12 months or six months. Under no circumstances shall be lump-sum so paid will be refundable would be making such payment subsequently resign the membership or cease to remain a member.
                    </b>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInLeft animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h2 class="bars" style="text-align:center">  THE MANAGING COMMITTEE</h2>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    a)      The Management of the Sabha shall be vested in a Managing Committee elected annually by the General Body and constituted as under:

                                    <br /><br />

                                    i)                    The President
                                    <br />
                                    ii)                  Two Vice Presidents (One permanently resident of Shimla & Delhi)
                                    <br />
                                    iii)                General Secretary
                                    <br />
                                    iv)                Two Joint Secretaries (One permanently resident of Shimla & Delhi)
                                    <br />
                                    v)                  One Treasurer & One Asstt. Treasurer (One permanently resident of Shimla & Delhi)
                                    <br />
                                    vi)                20 Members
                                    <br />
                                    This number shall, however be decreased or increased by the General Body as and when necessary.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    b) Sub-Committees
                                    <br /><br />
                                    The Managing Committee may appoint sub-committee with the personnel necessary to deal with the activities of Sabha.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    c)      A member of the Managing Committee who absents himself from three consecutive meetings of the committee without adequate reason shall seize to be a member of the committee.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    d)      Vacancies in the Committee
                                    <br /><br />
                                    i)              Officer bearers: Vacancies occurring among the office bearers during the course of the year normally be filled by the committee from among its members but may be filled by the committee from outside, subject to the confirmation of the General Body at its next meeting.
                                    <br />
                                    ii)            Members: Vacancies occurring among members shall be filled up by the Managing Committee until the next General Election.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>
                </table>

            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInRight animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center"> POWERS OF MANAGING COMMITTEE</h3>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    The Managing Committee shall have the following powers and perform the following duties:
                                    <br /><br />

                                    i)                    To make arrangements for the attainment of the objects of the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    ii)                  To see that the accounts due to the Sabha are properly and regularly realized and to sanction any expenditure incurred in connection with the activities of the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    iii)                To raise funds by sanction and other ways for any purpose or purposes so as to achieve the objects of the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    iv)                To make recommendations to the General Body regarding any change or addition to the rules contained herein.
                                    <br />
                                    v)                  To refuse admission to any person to become a member for sufficient grounds and to any person who does not before to Sabha for membership for special reason.
                                    <br />
                                    vi)                To promote
                                    <br />
                                    vii)              To present each year as the normal General Meeting a statement of Income and Expenditure for the preceeding duly audited by the Auditor of the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    viii)            In case that all moveable & immoveable property of the Sabha is properly looked after and inspected at suitable intervals.
                                    <br />
                                    ix)                To co-opt any person or member in any causal vacancy in the Managing Committee either by resignation or any other cause.
                                    <br />
                                    x)                  To do all other things that may be necessary for the efficient working of the Sabha.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>
                </table>

            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInLeft animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center"> DUTIES OF OFFICE BEARERS</h3>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    President : The President shall generally guide and supervise the affairs of the Sabha and shall preside at meetings of the General Body and of the Managing Committee. He may, however, at his discretion, propose any other distinguished person to preside at the meeting of the General Body.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    Vice President : The Vice-President shall function in place of the President in his absence.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    General Secretary : Subject to these rules, he shall be the Chief Executive Officer of the Sabha and shall have the following powers and duties:
                                    <br /><br />

                                    a)      He shall conduct the correspondence relating to all matters connected with the Sabha and too responsible for the maintenance for the records.
                                    <br />
                                    b)      He shall issue notice and keep minutes of all meetings.
                                    <br />
                                    c)      He shall exercise in accordance with the wishes of the Managing Committee, general supervision over affairs of the Sabha, including supervision of sub-committees functioning under the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    d)      He shall have powers to incur expenditure on the normal activities of the Sabha upto the extent of Rs.10/- provided the expenditure so incurred is reported to the Managing Committee at its next meeting for formal sanction.
                                    <br />
                                    e)      He shall be responsible for the collection of the subscriptions and other dues from the members.
                                    <br />
                                    f)       He shall prepare annually a report on the working of the Sabha & submit the same to the Managing Committee, prior to its presentation before the Annual General Meeting.
                                    <br />
                                    g)      He shall do such other things as may be required by the Managing Committee for the furtherance of the objects of the Sabha.
                                    <br /><br />
                                    Joint Secretary : The Joint Secretary shall assist the General Secy. And act for him during his absence.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    Treasurer : The treasurer shall have the following duties:
                                    <br /><br />
                                    a)      He shall be responsible for the proper realization of all the amounts due to the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    b)      He shall maintain proper accounts of all receipts and expenditure and submit to the Managing Committee through the General Secretary, statement of the income and expenditure for each month and an audited statement of the accounts for the year.
                                    <br />
                                    c)      He shall deposit all sums in the Post Office or bank excepting such amount as he may be authorized by the Managing Committee to retain on hand to meet current expenses.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    Asstt. Treasurer : The Assistance Treasurer shall assist the treasurer and act for him during his absence.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    Purpose of the Committee
                                    <br />
                                    For the efficient running of the Sabha the Managing Committee may allocate the various activities of the Sabha among its members.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>
                </table>

            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInRight animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center"> SABHA YEAR</h3>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    The Sabha year will be from the first of October to 30th September.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>
                </table>

            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInLeft animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center"> ACCOUNTS AND AUDIT</h3>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    a)      The accounts of the Sabha showing the inventory of the property of the Sabha be audited monthly by the auditor appointed by General Body and his report shall be submitted to the General Body in the Annual General Meeting alongwith the Annual Report and with any observations the managing committee may have to make thereon.
                                    <br /><br />
                                    b)      Financial Powers: Subject to these rules, the managing committee shall have full powers to regulate the financial affairs of the Sabha. The Managing Committee shall also have power to incur expenditure to the extent of the funds available under each head of account or on such items for which no provision exists, provided funds are made available by re-appropriation or otherwise.
                                    <br /><br />
                                    c)      Finance Sub-Committee: There shall be a Finance Sub-Committee consisting of three or more members to control the expenditure of the Sabha and to advise on all matters concerning the financial affairs of the Sabha.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid_3 grid_5 wow fadeInRight animated" data-wow-delay=".5s" style="margin-top:20px">
            <h3 class="bars" style="text-align:center"> MEETINGS</h3>
            <div class="bs-example">
                <table class="table">
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td colspan="2" class="type-info">
                                <p style="color:black; font-size:20px">
                                    General Body
                                    <br /><br />
                                    (i)                 Ordinary meetings: There shall be one meeting of the General Body towards the close of the Sabha year, at which the following business shall be transacted:
                                    <br /><br />
                                    (a)   The confirmation of the minutes of the last annual general meeting of the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    (b)   The gist of the annual report on the working of the Sabha during the preceding year, together with audited accounts and the auditorial report.
                                    <br />
                                    (c)    The election of the Managing Committee and one Auditor for the ensuing year.
                                    <br />
                                    (d)   The consideration of any other matter brought before the meeting, if allowed by the president.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    (ii)               Extraordinary Meetings: Extra-ordinary meetings of the General Body may be convened by the Managing Committee as and when necessary or shall be convened on a signed requisition from one-third of the members present at the station for the consideration of a specific question or questions. At such meetings only the question or questions mentioned in the requisition shall be transacted.

                                    <br /><br />
                                    (iii)             Quorum: The quorum for meetings shall be one-third of the number of members on the rolls on the date of the meeting and present at the station. Except as provided for in Rule-7 (a) the President, or in his absence the Vice-President shall be the Chairman of such meetings. If neither the President nor the Vice-President be present, the meeting shall elect its own Chairman. If within half an hour of the time appointed for the meeting, the quorum be not formed, the meeting may at the discretion of the Chairman be dissolved, if it was convened on the requisition of members. In other cases, it shall stand adjourned to a date to be fixed by the Managing Committee. The quorum shall be necessary for such adjourned meetings.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    (iv)              Notice: The General Secretary shall issue notice in the matter viz one month’s notice of ordinary annual meeting, the General Body and at least three days notice of extra ordinary meetings.
                                    <br /><br />
                                    <b>Note: This rule shall not apply to adjourned meetings in respect of which the General Secretary shall give as long a notice as he things fit.</b>
                                    <br /><br />

                                    (v)                Questions at General Meetings: At a general meeting a member may put questions on subject within the cognizance of Sabha, for the purpose of allotting information, subject to the following conditions:
                                    <br /><br />


                                    (a)   Notice of questions shall be sent to the Secretary in writing so as to reach him at least 12 hours before the time, the meeting is scheduled to be held. The President may, however, relax this restriction in any case for specific reasons.
                                    <br />
                                    (b)   Question shall be so framed as to be merely requests for information.
                                    <br />
                                    (c)    The Managing Committee may disallow a question on the ground that it cannot be answered consistently with the interests of Sabha, and their decisions shall be final. If however, such a question was not considered at a meeting of the Managing Committee, the President or Vice-President as the case may be shall exercise the power and he shall for any reason which need not be disclosed, disallow any question in the interests of the Sabha and such decision shall be final.
                                    <br />
                                    (d)   Question shall be asked by the person who gave notice thereof or in his absence by some of the authorized person at the discretion of the President.

                                    <br /><br />
                                    (vi)              Resignations at General Meetings: At a General Meeting a member may move resolution or bring forward motions, on matters relating to the works of the Sabha subject to the following conditions:
                                    <br /><br />
                                    (a)   A copy of the resolution to be sent to the General Secretary so as to reach him at least three clear days before the date of the meeting in special circumstances, however, the President may relax this condition.
                                    <br />
                                    (b)   Resolutions shall be moved or motions made in person by the member who gave notice there provided, however, that the President may in absence of that member, permit another duly authorized in writing to do so.
                                    <br />
                                    (c)    All motions, resolutions and amendments be duly proposed and seconded before being discussed.
                                    <br />
                                    (d)   Every motion shall be decided by major votes which the Chairman may take either of hands by ballot as he deems fit.
                                    <br />
                                    (e)   All members presents at a meeting shall have power to vote provided that no member on a matter in which his personal involvement in question. If any question arises as to the power of a member to vote, the ruling of the Chairman shall be final.
                                    <br />
                                    (f)     In case of equality of votes the Chairman shall have a casting vote.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    (vii)            MANAGING COMMITTEE

                                    <br /><br />

                                    (a)   Business Meetings: Meetings of the Committee shall be held as often as may be necessary or shall be convened on the requisition of six of its members for the consideration of any particular question or questions.
                                    <br />
                                    (b)   Notice: Notice of such meetings shall be sent by General Secretary at least 24 hours before the time fixed for the meeting.
                                    <br />
                                    (c)    Quorum: The quorum for meeting of the Managing Committee shall be seven, two of whom, at least shall be non office bearers. The President or in his absence, the Vice-President shall be the Chairman of such meetings. If neither the President nor the Vice-President be present, the meeting shall elect its own Chairman who shall not be either the General Secretary or Joint Secretary.
                                    <br />
                                    (d)   Casting Vote: The Chairman shall have a casting vote whenever the voting is equal.
                                    <br />
                                    (e)   Minutes: The Minutes of every meeting of the Managing Committee shall be confirmed at its next meeting.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    (viii)          DISCIPLINE

                                    <br /><br />

                                    The Managing Committee shall take cognizance of any infractions of these rules or of any circumstances likely to affect the good name of the Sabha or to cause annoyance to other members of the Sabha. Any serious breach of discipline on the part of member shall be brought to the notice of the General Body who may by a vote of consent of members present at the meeting and voting expel the member at fault from Sabha. The General Body may however, remit such member after a period of not less than six month from the date of such expulsion.
                                    <br /><br />

                                    (ix)              MISCELLANEOUS

                                    <br /><br />

                                    a)      Amendments to these rules shall ordinarily be considered at the Annual General Meeting.
                                    <br />
                                    b)      No amendments shall be made except on the vote of two-thirds of members present at a meeting of the General Body.
                                    <br />
                                    c)      Subject to the proviso of these rules the Managing Committee may frame such rules and bye-laws as are necessary for the efficient working of the different sub-committees under the control of the Sabha.
                                    <br />
                                    d)      In case of doubt, the power of interpretation of these rules shall vest in the Managing Committee.
                                    <br />
                                    e)      The Managing Committee shall have full discretion to act in any matter not provided for in these rules in the best of interests of the Sabha.
                                </p>
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>








    </div>
</div>
